ID:          5
Service:     service-b
Severity:    P1
Opened:      2026-05-29 16:27:58
Resolved:    2026-05-29 16:36:24
Title:       service-b degraded: FAILURE_THRESHOLD set to 0 (chaos mutation)
Report:      Root cause: uncommitted change in services/service-b/src/app.ts set FAILURE_THRESHOLD = 0 (was 3). The health check condition "consecutiveFailures >= FAILURE_THRESHOLD" evaluated true immediately (0 >= 0), so service-b always returned 503/degraded regardless of actual poll results. Compounded by persistent "RangeError: Invalid time value" failures in poll() caused by service-a's broken /time route (see incident #7).
Fix:         Restored const FAILURE_THRESHOLD = 3 in services/service-b/src/app.ts line 7.
QA:          Added regression test in services/service-b/src/__tests__/routes.test.ts: "stays ok with 2 consecutive failures (threshold boundary — regression for FAILURE_THRESHOLD=0 bug)" — asserts GET /health returns 200 + { status: "ok" } when consecutiveFailures < 3, directly catching any future FAILURE_THRESHOLD=0 mutation.
